#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / APT Specification
PACKAGE: apt
LANGUAGE: C++
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Package acquisition, dependency resolution, repository trust, transaction orchestration

## PROGRAM
APT is the high-level package-management layer. It consumes repository metadata, resolves dependencies, selects packages, and delegates local package installation to dpkg.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Ubuntu/Debian APT source
BOUNDARY: repository metadata -> trust validation -> dependency resolution -> transaction planning -> dpkg
WHITE_EDITION: overlay only; upstream provenance retained
GUI: optional JavaFX administration frontend; GUI never replaces APT transaction semantics

## SPEC
- repository trust must fail closed when required verification cannot be established
- package transactions must be observable and recoverable
- configuration must be deterministic and documented
- credentials and sensitive repository data must not enter ordinary diagnostics
- dependency resolution must preserve Debian/Ubuntu compatibility

## QUALITY
TEST: install, upgrade, remove, dependency resolution, invalid repository, interrupted transaction, recovery
ECONOMY: disk, memory, CPU, process count, transaction time, dependency expansion
PROMOTION: evidence required before source behavior changes

## SOURCE POLICY
Do not invent cryptographic primitives. Prefer existing APT/libapt-pkg mechanisms. Native C++ changes require focused regression tests and compatibility evidence.
